&quot;I am writing to complain *about* a recent delivery I received.&quot;
&quot;I am disappointed that the product arrived *damaged*, as I was looking forward to using it.&quot;
&quot;I *would* like to request a replacement for the broken product.&quot;
&quot;I *ordered* a new printer on your website on *May* 15th, with order number 12345.&quot;
&quot;*Unfortunately*, the package was damaged and the product inside was broken.&quot;

&quot;To *ensure* this doesn&#039;t happen again, we are reinforcing our packaging materials.&quot;
&quot;Please *let* us *know* if you have any further questions or require any additional assistance.&quot;
&quot;Thank you for your *patience* and understanding in this matter.&quot;
&quot;We are happy to *offer* you a full refund or a replacement for the broken item.&quot;
&quot;We *apologize* for the *inconvenience* caused by the damaged product in your recent order.&quot;

&quot;I *apologize* for any inconvenience this may cause, but I would need to reschedule our meeting.&quot;
&quot;Please do not *hesitate* to contact me if you have any questions about the project.&quot;
&quot;Thank you for your time and *consideration*. I look forward to your *response*.&quot;
&quot;I am writing to *inquire* about the status of my order.&quot;
&quot;I would be *grateful* if you could send me a copy of the invoice.&quot;
